Review of B4 · Differentiator (author: antigravity, commits d35d2a1 and 903420a)
by freebuff, 2026-10-16. Board head at start of review: e14a934 (lead's
R10/R11/board update). Spec: docs/work-orders.md "B4 · Differentiator".
Subject: mathd/src/differentiator.rs (312 lines), mathd/tests/differentiator.rs
(646 lines), mathd/fixtures/diff.json (766 cases), mathd/fixtures/generate.py
(+189 lines), mathd/src/lib.rs (+5 lines). Lead check (claude) comes after.

=== Method

- The repository was never edited. Every rust run used a scratch COPY of the
  mathd crate (cp -r, then tests/ and target/ removed from the copy). The
  pristine copy is byte-identical to the repo source:
  `diff temp/b4gate-sub/mathd/src/differentiator.rs mathd/src/differentiator.rs`
  -> no output, and `git status --short -- mathd/` was empty after every step.
  Three further scratch copies (A, B, C below) carry one deliberate break each.
- `cargo test` cannot link on this Windows host: `link: missing operand after
  '\377\376'` (a UTF-16 BOM reaches the linker as an argument; same failure as
  the lead's B3 review). No wasm32-wasip1 target and no wasmtime/wasmer are
  installed, so the subject's own Rust test binary could not be executed here.
  Instead: a throwaway wasm cdylib gate (temp/b4gate, outside the repo,
  wasm32-unknown-unknown, Node 24) exports run() and run_d() over the
  committed crate's parse / differentiate / eval_at. Breaks are compiled from
  broken scratch copies, never from an edited repo file.
- Part 1 is my own comparison loop, not the committed test code: every
  diff.json case is evaluated through the gate and compared with the same
  acceptance rule the committed test states (|got - want| <= 1e-10 *
  max(1, |want|)); error results must be failures, not skips.
- Part 2 is an independent central-finite-differences oracle: my own xorshift32
  RNG, my own expression generator (same operator/function set because the
  language is fixed, depth 3, exponents 1..3), points in [-3, 3] with |x| >=
  0.05, h = 1e-5. The skip rules, tolerance and bounds are replicated exactly
  from the committed test source (mathd/tests/differentiator.rs): skip when any
  of f(x), f(x+h), f(x-h) is undefined; skip when |f| > 1e6 (the rule that sees
  catastrophic-cancellation blindness of CFD at large magnitudes); skip when
  the second-difference estimate |f''| is non-finite or > 1e4 (lines 552-558
  region); skip when the symbolic derivative itself fails to evaluate; assert
  skip_count < total/2 (line 605) and tested_points >= 25_000 (line 612). The
  assert lines themselves could not run on this host; the LOGIC was executed
  against the real committed differentiator. This is stated as the limitation
  it is, not passed off as the real suite.
- diff.json provenance re-checked independently: header says generator
  mathd/fixtures/generate.py, sympy 1.14.0, mpmath 1.3.0, total 766; the
  cases array is 766. Regeneration was byte-identical (below).

