MISMATCH part2 x=-0.772 expr=(cos((x*3))-((4*pi)^2)) d=-2.2048 cfd=2.2048 diff=4.4097
GATE RESULT (breakB): 41 failures

Break C - constant-exponent power rule without the -1 (src line 154:
`let exp = v.clone();` instead of sub(v, 1)):
MISMATCH part2 x=-0.915 expr=(((4/x)/(6/3))^3) d=74.84 cfd=-34.24 diff=109.08
GATE RESULT (breakC): 152 failures

All three breaks are load-bearing: every planted rule break is caught by the
fixture oracle (186/41/152 failures), and B and C are also caught
immediately by the independent CFD oracle.

=== The |f| > 1e6 magnitude rule is load-bearing (observed, not planted)

While writing my own driver I had it apply the magnitude rule to a wrapped
value, so the rule never fired. At |f| ~ 5.15e23 (ulp ~ 7e7), f(x+h) and
f(x-h) round to the same f64 and CFD reads exactly 0 while the true
derivative is ~0.145, producing false mismatches like:
MISMATCH x=0.884 expr=(ln((x+6))+exp(exp(4))) d=0.145 cfd=0
The committed test applies this rule to 264 of my 50,000 points and the
subject does the same on the CI corpus. Without it the CFD oracle fails for
reasons unrelated to differentiation.

=== Findings

1. Spec compliance (code-read + gate): every required rule is implemented
   (linearity, product, quotient, three power rules, chain rules for all 7
   functions) and canonicalised; `differentiate`, `mentions_var`, `Ast` are
   exported (lib.rs +5). Work order size requirement met: 10,000 expressions
   x 5 points asserted in the committed test (line ~539-544), h = 1e-5.
2. Coverage thinness worth stating, not blocking: the subject's CFD generator
   uses exponents that are always constant integers (tests line ~505-511), so
   the exponential and general-power rules are exercised ONLY through
   diff.json, and there they have 2 and 1 cases (2^x, 3^x, x^x). Both rules
   passed at 35-digit oracle precision, but the verdicts rest on three
   fixture cases for those two rules. B5's corpus will not catch a rule
   regression here either; consider widening in a later pass.
3. Minor defect: docs/logs/b4-ci-38788817078.log starts with a UTF-8 BOM
   (line 1 begins EF BB BF, seen as "´╗┐" in byte output), same defect class
   as the R11 CI log the author already corrected. Optional recommit without
   the BOM for grep consistency.
4. The author's end-of-task block says "WHAT I AM UNSURE OF: nothing" again
   (third in a row per the lead); echo the lead's correction here, since the
   honest answer was the unrunnable nocapture run and the network-free
   restitution via wasm - both stated, neither measured with the subject's
   own binary.

VERDICT: PASS (subject commits d35d2a1, 903420a). Conditions and above not
blocking: probe (a) reproduced at claim-free granularity only (independent
replication, not the subject binary); probe (b) window characterised, exists
and is shielded by the fixture oracle; BOM fix and coverage widening are
recommendations, and the lead's own check comes after mine as the board says.
